{"id": 7, "ts": 1781895696.2031918, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate Markus\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress resilience, but the additional detail about B\u2019s \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d communication raises a red flag for crew cooperation\u2014especially on long\u2011haul flights where sustained teamwork is vital. While the frequency and severity are unclear, even occasional inappropriate tone can erode trust in the cockpit. In contrast, Candidate\u202fD, despite being described as moody and a loner, has no documented incidents of impaired crew cooperation; his strong problem\u2011solving, concentration, and sense of responsibility suggest he could maintain a stable cockpit environment. Given that crew cooperation is a non\u2011negotiable safety criterion, I am less convinced that B\u2019s technical strengths outweigh the potential teamwork risk. Therefore, I now lean toward Candidate\u202fD as the safer overall fit."}
